<title>BELGIUM: Unions call off third one-day Belgian rail strike.</title>
<headline>Unions call off third one-day Belgian rail strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian rail unions have called off a one-day train strike scheduled for Friday after talks with management that elicited promises of proper negotiations over reorganisation plans.</p>
<p>The strike, targetted on the Brussels region, would have paralysed all rail traffic in the country.</p>
<p>Rail unions have staged two 24-hour train strikes in the past two weeks in protest at the plans which principally divide the rail network into 15 different regions.</p>
<p>The unions, which have still not accepted the plans, fear they are in preparation for privatisation and could threaten jobs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
